        "metadata": {
          "category": "stories",
          "minAge": 6,
          "maxAge": 10,
          "media": {
            "duration": 2394,
            "fileSize": 19673950
          },
          "previewAudio": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0051/8845/2401/files/brain-bots-wildlife-defenders.mp3",
          "author": "Yoto",
          "seriestitle": "Brainbots",
          "description": "Meet the BrainBots: Nellie, Buzz, and Gibbs! When school closes, these high-tech knowledge-gathering robots come to life to find out as much information as they can for kids before the next school day starts. They can do some amazing stuff, too - think travelling back in time, shrinking all the way down to explore tiny spaces, and getting where humans can’t…\n\nBut what happens when they discover some missing data from the Central Information Hub?...\nIn this feature-length special the BrainBots are on an adventure of their own – gathering information about endangered species in order to update the Central Information Hub before it’s too late. But as they learn about the animals, they realise they don’t just want to update their knowledge… they want to help!\n\nJoin Nellie, Buzz and Gibbs as they explore some of our world’s endangered wildlife. From Humboldt Penguins, Rothschild Giraffes, Southern White Rhinos and Colombian Spider Monkeys, they’ll learn all about these animals and what’s being done to protect them. And most importantly - how we can help at home too!\n\nCreated in collaboration with the Chessington Wildlife Conservation, 20% of all profits will be donated to protecting endangered species.",
          "abridged": false,
          "accent": "US English",
          "audioPreviewUrl": "https://audio-previews-media.api.yotoplay.com/audio-previews/c2ac1595563a9857899a22457c1b13c0c963f359d4e88e8fb99f3d76def24d80/52gjywlCUIoPLmzEmLDaI7sKiZvfGATEGgukfRzhry4.mp3",
